WEBVTT

00:14.130 --> 00:19.670
I love it when screams of agony
are drowned out by the wind

00:19.670 --> 00:21.380
and become naught.

00:27.830 --> 00:30.500
But only if they're the screams of women.

00:31.330 --> 00:34.380
Wind, do you think so too?

00:36.170 --> 00:37.670
Of course you do.

00:38.170 --> 00:40.250
Your deaths won't lack meaning.

00:40.250 --> 00:43.960
You're showing me how much a human body
can be cut up and still live.

00:44.500 --> 00:50.880
You're the worthwhile diversion
strengthening the wind and I's sense of unity.

00:52.460 --> 00:55.210
Help me...

00:56.170 --> 00:58.250
Help, you say?

00:59.040 --> 01:00.580
Splendid idea.

01:01.830 --> 01:05.420
That's right. It would be wonderful
if someone came to help.

01:05.420 --> 01:09.170
Then the wind and I
won't fall prey to boredom.

01:10.630 --> 01:15.380
<b>Episode 3: Agitation</b>

01:14.080 --> 01:15.380
Listen up, you guys!

01:15.630 --> 01:17.460
This is where we need to stand firm!

01:17.460 --> 01:19.580
Let's show 'em what dragon hunters
are made of!

01:19.580 --> 01:20.380
Aye!

01:25.250 --> 01:27.540
What good are dragons hunters?

01:39.580 --> 01:41.540
Wh-who are you?

01:46.080 --> 01:47.330
I know!

01:48.170 --> 01:50.210
When it's all over, I'll slay you.

01:50.630 --> 01:52.000
Magnificent!

01:52.330 --> 01:54.130
Let us begin...

01:54.130 --> 01:56.670
the battle that will change
the fate of the world

01:57.330 --> 02:01.130
and the tale of how you and I
exterminate all dragons.

02:01.960 --> 02:03.330
Purururu!

02:03.330 --> 02:05.630
Wait a shecond!

02:07.790 --> 02:09.290
Pu!

02:11.540 --> 02:15.630
You're acting haughty in front of
the mashter, shtupid human!

02:16.040 --> 02:17.380
Slime.

02:17.790 --> 02:18.920
Long time no see.

02:19.710 --> 02:20.880
Pu!

02:20.880 --> 02:23.330
Don't get chummy with me!
Thish ish our firsht convershation!

02:23.670 --> 02:26.920
I'm the Dragon Monarch Crimshon's
number one shervant!

02:26.920 --> 02:29.040
I'm hish trushty Evil Shlime!

02:29.040 --> 02:32.630
A newbie needsh to show reshpect
by calling me Mishter Shlime!

02:32.630 --> 02:35.380
All right. Nice to meet you, Mister Slime.

02:35.380 --> 02:37.580
You're shpeaking too quietly!

02:37.580 --> 02:40.250
Shpeak up loud and clear-

02:42.330 --> 02:43.790
Can it, Slime.

02:44.630 --> 02:48.130
It's all well and good that you two
dummies are getting along,

02:48.130 --> 02:49.750
but more importantly,

02:49.750 --> 02:52.500
tell me about the future, Ragna.

02:52.710 --> 02:53.920
We lose.

02:53.920 --> 02:55.630
I'm well aware of that.

02:55.630 --> 02:57.130
What exactly happened?

02:57.500 --> 03:01.790
How many dragon monarchs did we slaughter?

03:03.170 --> 03:04.380
Come on!

03:04.580 --> 03:06.250
What about the World Magic?

03:06.960 --> 03:08.670
The Great Crusade?

03:09.250 --> 03:11.750
What happened to you in the end?

03:14.290 --> 03:18.420
My trust in you is swiftly plummeting,
all of a sudden.

03:18.420 --> 03:20.670
Are you sure about doing this?

03:20.670 --> 03:23.750
I do have vague memories,

03:23.750 --> 03:26.290
but I can't freely recall them.

03:26.540 --> 03:27.750
Oh?

03:28.040 --> 03:31.380
I didn't remember you right away either.

03:31.380 --> 03:33.750
I instantly remembered you
the moment I saw your face.

03:33.750 --> 03:39.170
Essentially, each of your memories need
a specific trigger in order to be recalled?

03:40.130 --> 03:41.000
Hah!

03:41.000 --> 03:43.000
How awfully convenient for you.

03:43.000 --> 03:46.250
And how awfully inconvenient for me.

03:46.250 --> 03:48.380
Do you distrust me, Crimson?

03:48.380 --> 03:52.330
Of course. The only person I trust is myself.

03:52.330 --> 03:54.210
Put your trust in me, Crimson.

03:54.210 --> 03:56.540
Then what about your power?

03:57.380 --> 04:00.500
The power your future self gave you.

04:00.500 --> 04:03.670
Don't tell me that's just a faint memory too.

04:03.920 --> 04:05.830
You don't need to worry about that!

04:05.830 --> 04:09.210
Silverine Battle Arts are in my body,
not my mind!

04:10.170 --> 04:11.330
Ragna!

04:12.420 --> 04:14.080
It's over, Crimson.

04:14.580 --> 04:18.130
I have a keen interest in
your Silverine Battle Arts.

04:18.500 --> 04:21.040
I want to see some dragons
get killed with them soon.

04:21.330 --> 04:24.460
Got it. Leave it to me. I'll kill as many as-

04:24.460 --> 04:25.460
No.

04:26.330 --> 04:28.670
You're not the one who will use them.

04:29.000 --> 04:30.460
I wanna go home!
They will.<b></b>

04:30.460 --> 04:34.210
You're okay now.
Our hometown is just across the border.

04:34.670 --> 04:38.130
We'll step in for your parents and
get you there safe and sound.

04:38.580 --> 04:40.210
I see.

04:43.290 --> 04:45.580
Fine folks, rest assured!

04:46.130 --> 04:49.130
We have already hunted
all the dragons nearby!

04:49.130 --> 04:50.790
It is now safe!

04:51.040 --> 04:54.500
This man here is known as
"Ragna the Reaper."

04:54.500 --> 04:58.420
He is a master dragon hunter who has
killed many superior dragons!

04:58.420 --> 04:59.290
Huh?

04:59.630 --> 05:01.000
The Reaper?

05:01.000 --> 05:02.500
I've never heard of him.

05:02.500 --> 05:03.580
Hey...

05:03.580 --> 05:06.330
And I am his companion,

05:06.330 --> 05:08.790
a humble mage.

05:08.790 --> 05:10.170
A mage?

05:10.170 --> 05:11.790
Seriously? No way!

05:11.790 --> 05:15.880
In this world, there is a skill known as magic.

05:16.210 --> 05:17.580
Most magic users are superior dragons

05:17.580 --> 05:20.290
who have a large amount of
magical ability in their blood.

05:20.670 --> 05:24.080
Very few humans who can use magic exist.

05:24.080 --> 05:28.250
Mages are so rare that most people
have heard of magic,

05:28.250 --> 05:32.210
but have never witnessed it being used.

05:32.210 --> 05:33.670
Consequently,

05:33.670 --> 05:35.380
these people are primed to be tricked!

05:35.380 --> 05:39.580
Th-then the water-like thing
that ate the dragon was...

05:39.580 --> 05:41.040
That was magic.

05:41.040 --> 05:44.750
Then when that water stuff
turned into a person, that was...

05:44.750 --> 05:45.960
Eh?

05:46.330 --> 05:47.580
Magic.

05:47.580 --> 05:49.830
Hey! Shtupid humansh!

05:49.830 --> 05:51.040
It can talk?

05:51.040 --> 05:53.750
This is my pet that I made out of magic.

05:53.750 --> 05:55.080
Purun.

05:56.290 --> 05:58.790
Whoa, magic is awesome!

05:59.040 --> 06:01.580
Magic is awesome.

06:01.960 --> 06:03.960
All right, everyone join in!

06:03.960 --> 06:05.460
Magic is awesome!

06:06.170 --> 06:08.080
M-magic is...

06:08.500 --> 06:10.250
All together now.

06:10.250 --> 06:12.960
Magic is awesome! Okay!

06:13.250 --> 06:14.830
Magic is awesome!

06:14.960 --> 06:16.540
Magic is awesome!

06:16.710 --> 06:18.080
Magic is awesome!

06:18.080 --> 06:19.630
One more time!

06:19.630 --> 06:20.920
Magic is awesome!

06:21.040 --> 06:22.170
Magic is awesome!

06:22.290 --> 06:23.500
Magic is awesome!

06:23.750 --> 06:25.580
Magic is awesome!

06:33.460 --> 06:36.540
Mr. Reaper, Mr. Mage.

06:36.540 --> 06:39.330
My name is Michael.
I'm a dragon hunter.

06:39.330 --> 06:40.540
Nevertheless...

06:43.580 --> 06:46.630
I have a shameful request to make.

06:47.750 --> 06:50.670
There is a dragon only you two can take down.

06:51.080 --> 06:52.420
A dragon, you say?

06:52.420 --> 06:55.920
Yes. We ran away.

06:56.670 --> 07:00.830
There was a massive tornado
in the city Tortiere.

07:01.630 --> 07:03.710
Wh-what is that?

07:05.040 --> 07:07.040
And I had the distinct feeling...

07:07.830 --> 07:13.540
that something terrible was within
the tornado's winds.

07:14.920 --> 07:18.460
The Third Seat.
The Tempest Cell, Disas Trois.

07:18.460 --> 07:20.540
A dragon who cloaks himself in wind.

07:20.540 --> 07:21.750
You know about him?

07:22.000 --> 07:24.080
Naturally. I'm a mage.

07:27.420 --> 07:28.880
Where are you going?

07:28.880 --> 07:30.170
Hunting.

07:30.170 --> 07:31.290
No, you aren't.

07:31.630 --> 07:34.040
Or rather, you can't.

07:38.750 --> 07:40.580
Wh-what's happening?

07:43.500 --> 07:47.500
Do you know why you can't get up?

07:48.920 --> 07:50.080
Muscle soreness.

07:50.080 --> 07:52.210
You've eliminated the limits
of your mind, correct?

07:53.670 --> 07:57.540
I'm aware that your body physically
cannot keep unless you do that.

07:57.540 --> 08:00.880
But you've been pushing yourself too hard.

08:00.880 --> 08:03.580
All your body's muscle fibers are too damaged.

08:03.580 --> 08:05.790
I imagine you won't be able
to move for three days.

08:05.790 --> 08:07.830
Sh-shit!

08:09.000 --> 08:11.750
Just leave this to me.

08:11.750 --> 08:14.790
What did I tell you?
I'm going to use them.

08:16.130 --> 08:20.380
I'm sorry to report that the Reaper
is injured and cannot move.

08:20.380 --> 08:21.580
That's terrible!

08:21.580 --> 08:23.250
Is there anything we can do?

08:23.380 --> 08:24.580
There isn't.

08:24.580 --> 08:27.670
If he pushes himself too hard now, it will
negatively affect his dragon-hunting career.

08:27.670 --> 08:31.460
If that's the case, Mr. Mage,
instead could you-

08:31.460 --> 08:32.790
I decline.

08:32.790 --> 08:34.290
We'll pay you.

08:34.290 --> 08:36.420
We'll even sell our equipment if we have to.

08:36.420 --> 08:38.040
Name your price!

08:38.290 --> 08:39.670
Oh-ho.

08:39.670 --> 08:41.420
They'll give up their weapons?

08:41.420 --> 08:44.290
Which means they don't intend
to continue dragon hunting.

08:45.330 --> 08:48.170
Well, I can't have that.

08:48.540 --> 08:50.380
I decline.

08:50.380 --> 08:55.790
First of all, why are you so concerned
about the Tempest Cell?

08:56.460 --> 09:00.040
It doesn't seem like your lives
are currently at stake.

09:01.330 --> 09:04.210
Couldn't you just give up and run away?

09:04.210 --> 09:06.420
You're not from this country, right?

09:06.420 --> 09:09.710
You don't have any obligation
to fight for this country.

09:10.920 --> 09:14.920
You offered to pay me, not to protect you,

09:14.920 --> 09:18.960
but to kill the dragon for you.
What a peculiar request.

09:18.960 --> 09:21.130
Ah, I get it now.

09:21.130 --> 09:23.630
You guys feel guilty.

09:25.710 --> 09:28.500
The Tempest Cell's attack range is wide.

09:28.500 --> 09:30.330
And he moves quickly.

09:30.330 --> 09:37.000
To escape from him, you must make
snap decisions and flee as quickly as possible.

09:37.290 --> 09:40.210
That's what I'd imagine, anyway.

09:41.500 --> 09:45.290
As you fled, did you hear voices
behind you calling for help?

09:45.460 --> 09:46.750
"Let me ride with you!"

09:46.750 --> 09:47.830
"Wait!"

09:47.830 --> 09:48.960
"Please!"

09:48.960 --> 09:50.380
"Don't go!"

09:50.540 --> 09:54.250
Then those cries were swallowed up
by the wind and abruptly went silent.

09:54.500 --> 10:00.040
By the way, if you were wondering what happens
to people who get engulfed by the maelstrom,

10:00.040 --> 10:03.330
the cutting winds mangle their bodies,

10:03.330 --> 10:06.380
and they suffer hellish agony,
as I understand it.

10:06.380 --> 10:08.630
Hence the name Tempest Cell.

10:09.130 --> 10:11.460
When you escaped from the tornado,

10:11.460 --> 10:14.500
didn't blood suddenly
rain down from the sky?

10:14.500 --> 10:16.040
Splat.

10:21.250 --> 10:23.710
You must have felt guilty.

10:24.290 --> 10:25.500
His voice...

10:25.920 --> 10:28.290
You were ashamed.

10:28.290 --> 10:32.130
Thus, you gathered up the people
who were still alive,

10:32.130 --> 10:35.960
and escaped to this place,
trying to at least protect them.

10:35.960 --> 10:38.580
His voice is burrowing into my mind!

10:38.580 --> 10:40.790
But in the end...

10:40.790 --> 10:42.750
Stop! Please stop!

10:47.000 --> 10:49.880
Everything you said is true.

10:49.880 --> 10:52.000
But what else could we have done?

10:52.000 --> 10:55.130
How could hunters like us
even nick a superior dragon once?

10:55.130 --> 10:59.920
A dragon hunter's job is to protect people
from dragons with a single silver weapon.

10:59.920 --> 11:02.170
Did you not take pride in that?

11:02.540 --> 11:07.500
Yeah. I might have used to feel that way.

11:09.080 --> 11:11.080
I just realized something.

11:11.080 --> 11:12.880
I'm not a dragon hunter!

11:12.880 --> 11:14.920
I'm just prey!

11:15.830 --> 11:22.080
But if I had the power to hurt the dragons,
power like you two have, then I'd...!

11:28.130 --> 11:29.250
Oh!

11:33.290 --> 11:36.130
Do you finally understand
what I'm getting at?

11:36.130 --> 11:38.130
This is the power you desire.

11:38.460 --> 11:44.080
With this Reaper Sword, I guarantee
you'll be able to kill dragons too.

11:44.670 --> 11:49.080
That being said,
I make no guarantee you'll live.

11:50.210 --> 11:54.040
Will you bear this blade?

12:00.710 --> 12:03.670
Do you want to be dragon hunters?

12:04.000 --> 12:07.670
Your will to fight is commendable!

12:09.080 --> 12:11.750
<b>Tortiere</b>

12:14.040 --> 12:15.580
I guess this will do.

12:24.170 --> 12:26.920
All right, go ahead. Come on in.

12:35.920 --> 12:38.630
H-how is this possible?

12:39.460 --> 12:40.580
Magic.

12:40.580 --> 12:42.710
Magic is awesome!

12:45.290 --> 12:47.630
I've never seen a gun like this.

12:47.630 --> 12:49.630
Is this a magic gun?

12:49.880 --> 12:54.710
These guns are by far more powerful than
the ones currently available in this country,

12:54.710 --> 12:56.880
but they're still just regular guns.

12:57.080 --> 13:00.130
What's important are...

13:00.130 --> 13:01.580
the bullets.

13:08.290 --> 13:09.830
Done.

13:09.830 --> 13:12.170
Okay, now do this one.

13:18.460 --> 13:19.580
Ha ha!

13:19.580 --> 13:21.630
This gun is sick!

13:21.630 --> 13:24.040
You've got an impish look
on your face, Crimson.
It's totally a magic gun!<b></b>

13:24.040 --> 13:25.170
Hm?
These will do the trick!<b></b>

13:25.170 --> 13:29.040
Says the guy with the sullen look on his face.
With these, we've got this in the bag!<b></b>

13:30.500 --> 13:31.790
Are you displeased with something?
Yeah! Let's kill the dragons!<b></b>

13:31.790 --> 13:34.040
Is it that I'm using them as pawns?
Yeah! Let's kill the dragons!<b></b>

13:34.290 --> 13:37.040
No. I'm not upset about that.

13:37.040 --> 13:40.580
After all, you'll make sure they win, right?

13:41.880 --> 13:44.960
Well, I didn't promise they'd survive.

13:45.460 --> 13:47.330
So what are you upset about?

13:48.290 --> 13:52.130
Firstly, I'm so exhausted
that I'm stuck lying on the ground.

13:52.540 --> 13:54.830
And secondly, well...

13:56.920 --> 14:01.250
Please don't call me "Reaper"
and make a spectacle out of me.

14:01.500 --> 14:02.790
Master Reaper!

14:02.790 --> 14:05.210
Please protect us!

14:10.130 --> 14:11.710
I don't...

14:11.710 --> 14:14.080
I don't want them to be around me.

14:14.500 --> 14:17.000
Because then they might die.

14:19.330 --> 14:21.170
You said you only can be around people

14:21.170 --> 14:24.580
whose deaths won't hurt you
or people who won't die.

14:24.790 --> 14:27.540
That's why you chose me,

14:27.540 --> 14:30.830
and that's why you abandoned that girl, Leo.

14:30.830 --> 14:32.040
I didn't aband-

14:32.040 --> 14:33.420
You did abandon her.

14:34.000 --> 14:36.250
That's what happened from
an objective viewpoint,

14:36.250 --> 14:39.500
and she probably subjectively felt like
that's what you did too.

14:40.880 --> 14:42.960
That's none of your business.

14:42.960 --> 14:44.580
It certainly is!

14:44.580 --> 14:47.750
That girl is your entire motivation.

14:47.750 --> 14:49.920
What will happen to you if you lose her?

14:51.420 --> 14:54.750
You will exterminate all of dragonkind.

14:54.750 --> 14:57.920
I won't let you call it quits before
we've accomplished just that.

14:58.420 --> 15:03.210
Now that we're working together,
Leo is highly important to me too.

15:03.210 --> 15:05.290
If you have any concerns, spit 'em out.

15:07.920 --> 15:09.960
Logically speaking,

15:09.960 --> 15:14.380
I know that keeping Leo close to me
would be the best way to protect her.

15:14.710 --> 15:18.130
Keeping her far away from me
doesn't necessarily mean she'll be safe.

15:19.790 --> 15:21.040
But...

15:22.130 --> 15:23.710
I'm afraid.

15:24.960 --> 15:28.920
What if I lose Leo
right before my eyes again?

15:29.790 --> 15:31.750
The mere thought of that...

15:33.750 --> 15:36.170
almost breaks my heart.

15:37.830 --> 15:40.750
Thank you for opening up to me.

15:41.420 --> 15:43.880
I understand you a little better now.

15:43.880 --> 15:45.170
That pleases me.

15:45.880 --> 15:47.880
Crimson?

15:50.380 --> 15:53.380
Well, I'll give you a tidbit of Crimson advice!

15:53.380 --> 15:54.210
Huh?

15:54.540 --> 15:56.630
Hold Leo captive.

15:58.170 --> 16:00.290
I've got my storage spaces, right?

16:00.290 --> 16:02.380
I'll open one up for you.

16:02.380 --> 16:04.500
Lock her up there.

16:04.500 --> 16:08.460
Drug her up and put her in a comatose state
so she doesn't struggle.

16:08.460 --> 16:12.960
She'll sleep in a safe place until
we've exterminated all the dragons.

16:12.960 --> 16:17.080
Then she won't be dragged into your battles,

16:17.080 --> 16:20.210
and she won't die in an unknown location.

16:20.210 --> 16:23.880
You can take care of her while she sleeps.

16:23.880 --> 16:26.580
You like doing that, do you not?

16:26.580 --> 16:30.290
I gotta hand it to myself!
That was excellent, A-plus advice!

16:30.290 --> 16:32.250
I'll have her kidnapped immedia-

16:32.250 --> 16:33.630
Whoa there!

16:35.710 --> 16:39.420
Your muscle soreness is at its peak!
That weak-ass punch won't work!

16:39.420 --> 16:41.630
There! Right in the liver!

16:43.790 --> 16:45.420
Good grief.

16:45.420 --> 16:49.500
I've kindly given you such wonderful
words of wisdom, but you won't listen.

16:50.750 --> 16:52.170
What's your problem?

16:52.170 --> 16:53.290
Tell me.

16:53.290 --> 16:56.750
My problem is that you're a real asshole!

16:56.750 --> 16:58.380
People tell me that a lot.

16:58.380 --> 17:01.130
I think it's one of my strong points.
Whatcha think?

17:01.130 --> 17:05.580
Knowing I'm an asshole and
me truly putting you through hell

17:05.580 --> 17:08.250
are two entirely different things, huh?

17:08.830 --> 17:13.920
I've hated your "I know so much about you"
attitude ever since we met.

17:13.920 --> 17:15.380
Know your place.

17:15.830 --> 17:18.920
You don't know anything about me.

17:23.750 --> 17:27.830
Don't worry. I'll crush the Tempest Cell.

17:27.830 --> 17:30.000
I don't like putting my pawns to waste.

17:30.790 --> 17:34.380
You can lie there with your breaking heart

17:34.380 --> 17:37.170
and struggle to infuse bullets
with your silverine.

17:37.170 --> 17:38.710
Oh, and also...

17:38.710 --> 17:42.210
You've gone on a lot about
how you're cursed.

17:42.210 --> 17:43.670
You're wrong.

17:43.960 --> 17:45.330
A curse...

17:54.420 --> 17:56.750
Is more like this.

17:57.670 --> 17:59.630
You're not cursed.

18:01.330 --> 18:05.330
Don't ever put on the tragic act
and lament about being cursed again.

18:07.960 --> 18:08.960
Puru!

18:09.210 --> 18:11.210
Mashter Crimshon!

18:11.460 --> 18:12.630
How did it go?

18:12.630 --> 18:17.080
Perfectly! I extended one of my eyes down
to shpy on the town jusht like you shaid!

18:17.080 --> 18:18.710
Good job.

18:18.710 --> 18:20.420
I'll give you my corpse as your reward.

18:20.420 --> 18:22.960
Thank you sho much, Mashter!

18:22.960 --> 18:24.630
I'll shavor every morshel!

18:24.630 --> 18:25.830
Now, show me.

18:26.000 --> 18:27.710
Yesh, Mashter!

18:27.710 --> 18:30.130
Thish ish what the town
currently looksh like!

18:30.130 --> 18:32.080
It ish a heap of rubble!

18:32.080 --> 18:35.170
A vortex ish in the middle of town!

18:35.170 --> 18:38.040
The Tempesht Shell ish in it!

18:38.040 --> 18:42.540
Alsho, there are lotsh of humansh
floating in front of the tornado!

18:42.540 --> 18:43.460
Ah.

18:43.460 --> 18:45.000
There are shixteen in total.

18:45.000 --> 18:47.670
They're covered in blood
and don't have all their limbsh!

18:47.670 --> 18:49.000
Are they all women?

18:49.000 --> 18:50.500
Puru! Yesh, they are!

18:51.540 --> 18:55.080
Trois has been ordered to
stand by in that town

18:55.080 --> 18:58.420
and is killing time by carving them up.

18:58.420 --> 19:00.540
What a pathetic twit.

19:00.920 --> 19:05.790
But at least as long as he's entertaining
himself, he won't come this way.

19:06.210 --> 19:10.380
I need those women to hang in there
as long as possible.

19:10.380 --> 19:11.670
Pururu!

19:11.670 --> 19:14.670
Mashter Crimshon,
you're alwaysh a delishious meal!

19:14.670 --> 19:18.250
I can't let Ragna and the dragon hunters
know about this.

19:18.250 --> 19:21.170
There are no survivors in town.

19:21.170 --> 19:24.040
That's all they need to know.
This will work.

19:31.000 --> 19:33.670
I've devised a plan to hunt the Tempest Cell.

19:33.670 --> 19:34.750
Huh?

19:39.210 --> 19:41.250
Today is a day that will go down in history.

19:41.670 --> 19:45.380
Today will be remembered as the day
true dragon hunting was born in this country.

19:45.830 --> 19:47.540
Bring down the Tempest Cell.

19:47.540 --> 19:48.880
Burn him in the sunlight.

19:49.170 --> 19:53.170
Let us begin the history of
the true dragon hunters!

20:00.210 --> 20:01.710
Really?

20:01.710 --> 20:04.580
Ah, so you have come.

20:04.580 --> 20:07.000
It's a bit late to help now though.

20:09.130 --> 20:10.540
Welcome.

20:10.880 --> 20:13.420
The wind sends its greetings too.

20:13.420 --> 20:16.130
But unfortunately, it's nearly dawn.

20:16.130 --> 20:18.580
My apologies, but you'll have to
come back lat-

20:19.540 --> 20:21.040
Ahem!

20:22.540 --> 20:24.710
We are dragon hunters!

20:24.710 --> 20:26.920
This is such a pleasant morning!

20:26.920 --> 20:32.290
The perfect morning to hunt an vile dragon
that has committed acts of utmost cruelty!

20:32.580 --> 20:35.420
And when I say "vile dragon,"
I'm talking about you!

20:35.420 --> 20:37.920
The cringy one pretending to
chitchat with the wind

20:37.920 --> 20:41.000
when he's really just putting on
a one-man show!

20:41.250 --> 20:47.710
The pathetic one ordered to stand by
in this remote place by your nutty ruler!

20:48.040 --> 20:50.920
We pity you, so we'll play with you.
Follow us.

20:52.880 --> 20:54.210
Me?

20:54.210 --> 20:55.540
Pathetic?

20:56.250 --> 20:57.920
What are you talking about?

20:57.920 --> 20:59.130
Who even are you?

20:59.130 --> 21:01.920
Why is a lowly human blathering on
about our bloodline?

21:01.920 --> 21:03.790
I find that pretending to know about subjects
you know nothing about is embarrassing.

21:03.790 --> 21:04.790
I suggest you stop.

21:04.790 --> 21:07.080
To start, are you even capable of
fully comprehending my greatness?

21:07.080 --> 21:07.920
You can't, correct?

21:07.920 --> 21:10.170
If you were capable, you wouldn't say
such things. How do I know that?

21:10.170 --> 21:13.000
I'm Disas Trois, the Third Seat
of the Blood of the Wing.

21:13.000 --> 21:14.880
The Third Seat means I'm third from the top.

21:14.880 --> 21:15.790
Do you understand? You don't?

21:15.790 --> 21:17.750
You're dim-witted, huh? Then I'll elaborate.

21:17.750 --> 21:22.210
According to a rumor I heard from the wind,
some humans call me the Tempest Cell.

21:22.210 --> 21:24.130
Apparently, I've been dubbed this

21:24.130 --> 21:26.460
because humans who dance with
my winds suffer hellish agony.

21:26.460 --> 21:27.540
This vexes me.

21:27.540 --> 21:29.330
I don't believe what I'm doing
is all that abhorrent,

21:29.330 --> 21:30.630
and the wind certainly isn't at fault.

21:30.630 --> 21:32.040
If anything, humans should become
more adept at frolicking in the wind.

23:05.210 --> 23:10.420
I will forgive your ignorant,
boorish remarks from earlier.

23:11.290 --> 23:14.000
But I cannot forgive anything else!

23:14.000 --> 23:16.540
Your insults to our bloodline
cannot be forgiven!

23:16.790 --> 23:18.880
"Nutty," you said?

23:18.880 --> 23:21.580
You called our progenitor nutty!

23:21.580 --> 23:26.580
Our sovereign, the leader of our bloodline
who hears the voice of God!

23:26.920 --> 23:29.330
The likes of a human dared to slight them!

23:29.330 --> 23:30.830
Absolutely reprehensible!

23:30.830 --> 23:32.460
Heads will absolutely roll!

23:32.460 --> 23:35.080
Heads will roll! Heads will roll!
Heads will roll! Heads will roll!

23:35.380 --> 23:40.080
The wind itself ordains it sooooo!

23:40.380 --> 23:41.580
Too gullible.

23:42.380 --> 23:45.040
Everyone, the morning sun is rising!

23:47.790 --> 23:49.790
The battle shall begin.
